    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner `email` support end-to-end, following the existing Spring conventions (the same pattern used for `telephone` normalization).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema with `format: email` and a `pattern` (`^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`). Since the generator runs with `performBeanValidation`, this produces `@Email` + `@Pattern` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`, so a present-but-invalid email is rejected by Bean Validation \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400** (via the existing `ExceptionControllerAdvice`). Being optional (not in `required`), a missing email is accepted.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added an `email` column, getter/setter, and a `toString` entry. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` auto-maps the matching `email` field in both directions.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added the `email` column to the `owners` table in the hsqldb (used by tests), h2, mysql, and postgres `schema.sql` files. The hsqldb `data.sql` used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I gave those inserts an explicit column list so the seed data still loads.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeEmail` helper that lower-cases a non-null email, and applied it in both `addOwner` and `updateOwner` so the value is stored and returned in canonical lower-case form.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The three acceptance checkpoints (lower-cases email, rejects invalid email with 400, accepts missing email) all pass.",
